FEX on Android: mkdir, rmdir and unlink of RootFS-only directories.

mkdir, mkdirat, rmdir, unlink and unlinkat go to the host first. When that fails with ENOENT or
ENOTDIR for an absolute path whose parent does not exist on the host but resolves in the RootFS
(OpenInRoot, patch 0002), the call is made relative to that RootFS directory. Wine's server
directory /tmp/.wine-<uid> needs it: Android has no /tmp, the RootFS has. mkdirat and unlinkat
move from the plain passthroughs to Syscalls/FS.cpp.

